# MadGraph5 batch script: e+ e- > mu+ mu- ta+ ta- at LO, QCD=0
#
# Minimal pure-EW (γ/Z) continuum process that exercises a CHAINED off-shell
# fermion current — the HELAS path that ee→μμ (2→2) never touches but the
# uux 2→6 continuum does. The incoming e-line absorbs two internal off-shell
# γ/Z bosons in series (one →μ⁺μ⁻, one →τ⁺τ⁻), so an off-shell fermion current
# (fvixxx/fvoxxx) consumes an off-shell vector propagator current.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Colorless (all leptons) => no color factor (CF=1), unlike uux (Nc²=9).
#   - Three DISTINCT fermion lines (e, mu, ta) => no identical final-state
#     particles and no relative Fermi sign needed (no crossing lines).
#   - Massless leptons under the SM restriction => pure γ/Z continuum, no Higgs
#     (zero Yukawa), bit-for-bit comparable to vibegraph (same param_card).
#
# This isolates the uux continuum relative-phase bug in a 3-line / 2→4 process,
# far smaller than the 4-line / 2→6 uux, enabling per-diagram AMP() comparison.
generate e+ e- > mu+ mu- ta+ ta- QCD=0
output ee_to_mumu_tata_qcd0 -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
